## Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

Successfully implemented Vercel Web Analytics for this React + Vite project.

### Changes Made

**1. Package Installation**
   - Installed `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 using npm
   - Package added to dependencies in package.json

**2. Code Integration (src/App.tsx)**
   - Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/react';`
   - Added `<Analytics />` component at the end of the main app div, right after the CustomAgentModal
   - Placement follows official Vercel documentation for React applications

**3. Files Modified**
   - `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
   - `package-lock.json` - Updated with new dependency tree
   - `src/App.tsx` - Added Analytics import and component

### Implementation Details

Following the latest official Vercel Analytics documentation (fetched from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart), this implementation:
- Uses the React-specific package export (`@vercel/analytics/react`)
- Places the Analytics component at the root level of the application
- Ensures analytics tracking across all routes managed by React Router

### Verification

✅ Build completed successfully (`npm run build`)
✅ TypeScript type checking passed with no errors
✅ No build artifacts or cache files staged

### Next Steps

After deployment to Vercel:
1. Analytics will automatically start tracking page views
2. Data will appear in the Vercel dashboard after a few days of visitor activity
3. The integration will add routes scoped at `/_vercel/insights/*`
4. You can verify the setup by checking for Fetch/XHR requests to the analytics endpoint in browser Network tab

### Notes

- The Analytics component is lightweight and won't impact application performance
- It integrates seamlessly with React Router for automatic route tracking
- No additional configuration is required - analytics will work out of the box when deployed to Vercel
